Z||000021||Toddster||05-30-2001||04:34 PM||||Canadian GT, there WAS a front bra option issued by the factory through the dealer network.<P>Factory Bras are exceedingly rare. I found one in a wrecking yard years ago. Since then I've found many aftermarket variety but never another factory bra.<P>It is distinguised by two things: It came in a blue vinyl storage bag and it had clear plastic blinker lens covers. <P>It was a cumbersome design with metal clasps and velcro. I keep mine for nastolga sake. I would never use it on a car.<P>The best Bra on the market is clearly the Colgan Custom bra. They are located in Fountain Valley, California and can UPS one to you in no time. The quality is superior with tough stitching, easy installation, and a snug fit.<P>They don't screen the 'Fiero' logo or name on them anymore but older bras came with it.<p>[This message has been edited by Toddster (edited 05-30-2001).]||||reg||1
